"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act1_ch4.md — do not edit */

SC["c2_open"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER FOUR — GRANNY`)+((G.sho>=2)?(P(`Granny Sho listened to the whole impossible story that night without once calling it impossible. When you finished she was quiet for a long time, and then she said: “Forty years ago my sworn sister glowed like you. The mountain ate her. Sweep near me, gold-thread. I have things to teach a boy with no meridians.”`)):(P(`Granny Sho smiled at your lie that night the way grandmothers smile at lies, and shuffled off into the dark. But the next morning your name is on the courtyard-sweeping roster in a hand nobody recognizes, and the old woman sweeping beside you says nothing at all — which is, you will come to understand, an open door.`)))+DIV+P(`Autumn comes to the mountain like a decision. The maple on the third terrace goes over in one night, the wash-water starts biting, and your education begins — disguised, like everything else down here, as chores.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Sweep near the old woman. See what the broom is really for.`,go:"a1c4_sweeping"}]};

SC["a1c4_sweeping"]={t:()=>P(`“You sweep like a thief,” Granny Sho says, the first morning. “Snatching. The courtyard isn't yours to take.” Tap, goes the cane. “Again. With it this time, not across it.”`)+P(`It takes you four mornings to understand she isn't talking about leaves. The courtyard has a grain — threads laid down by a century of feet and weather and the slow silver pulse of the dragon vein under the flagstones — and there is a way of moving through it that rumples the weave, and a way that smooths it. She can't see your threads. She <i>hears</i> them, somehow, the way you'd hear a wrong note in the next room.`)+P(`“Old woman,” you ask, on a morning when the frost has emptied the yard of witnesses, “what am I sweeping?”`)+P(`“The same thing I am,” she says. “You with your eyes. Me with what's left.” Tap. “Again.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Practice until moving-with becomes the only way you move.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);note("The Weave stops being a thing you look at. It starts being a place you stand.");},go:"a1c4_sister"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Ask her, carefully, what it costs to hear what she hears.`,do:()=>{G.sho++;addStat("heart",1);note("Granny Sho +1. She goes still, and the next morning's lesson starts somewhere much older.");},go:"a1c4_sister"}]};

SC["a1c4_sister"]={t:()=>P(`She tells it the way you'd clean a wound — in three nights, a little at a time, never looking at it directly.`)+P(`The first night it's just a name without a name: <i>my sworn sister</i>, a girl Sho grew up beside in the wash-yards, sixty years ago. “She glowed,” Sho says. “Not to eyes. To the inside of the day. Rooms were better with her in them, and nobody could say why.” The second night it's the hunger: how the girl rose — wash-yard to outer court to inner, faster than anyone, because something in her simply <i>worked</i> that didn't work in other people. “They said spirit roots. They tested her three times because they couldn't find any.”`)+P(`The third night, Sho sweeps for an hour first, and then says, to the courtyard rather than to you: “The night the mountain ate her, I heard it. The only time in my life. A sound like — a loom, working. Big as weather. I ran toward it, and there was gold light under the door of a hall that hasn't existed since, and I listened at that door, boy. I listened with everything I had.” Tap. The cane is not steady. “What I had was the price. Woke up blind, with her gone, and forty years of being told there was never any such hall.”`)+P(`She turns her white eyes on you, and for once they are exactly aimed.`)+P(`“Then a kitchen boy ties a knot in the dark, and the courtyard sings like her laugh. So I'll ask you once more, gold-thread, and this time I've earned it: what do you intend to be on this mountain?”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`“I'm going home. Whatever it takes, I'm going home.”`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_intent="home";},go:"a1c4_gift"},
  {id:"c1",l:`“Strong enough that nothing on this mountain can eat anyone I know.”`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_intent="strong";},go:"a1c4_gift"},
  {id:"c2",l:`“Whoever ate her is still eating. I intend to find out who. And stop them.”`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_intent="even";},go:"a1c4_gift"},
  {id:"c3",l:`“Alive. Unnoticed. Safe. I've died once already.”`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_intent="safe";},go:"a1c4_gift"}]};

SC["a1c4_gift"]={t:()=>((G.f.a1_intent==="home")?(P(`Sho nods slowly. “Home,” she repeats, like a word she's checking for cracks. “Then learn fast. Doors that close between worlds don't wait on slow students.”`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent==="strong")?(P(`Sho's mouth does something that an optimist would call a smile. “Good answer. Wrong, but good. Strength doesn't keep people, boy. But you'll learn that the way everyone does.”`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent==="even")?(P(`For a long moment the only sound is wind in the bare maple. “Forty years,” Sho says at last, very quietly, “I have swept this yard waiting to hear someone say that out loud.” Tap. “Mind it doesn't eat you instead.”`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent==="safe")?(P(`“Safe.” Sho laughs, one dry leaf of a laugh. “A boy who glows, on this mountain, safe. Well — honest, at least. Stay near the kitchens, gold-thread. Nothing hunts near Tang's cleaver.”`)):(""))+((G.sho>=2)?(P(`That night she teaches you the breathing.`)+P(`It isn't a technique. It's older and stranger than that — a way of letting the body idle so that the attention can go all the way out along the threads, the way her hearing goes out. “My sister's,” she says simply. “She made it up. Somebody should be using it.” By the third dawn your reach is wider, your knots surer, and the budget of held tension in your chest has learned to refill from the mountain itself.`)+SYS(`Sho's sister's breathing-form, forty years in trust, paid forward.`)):(P(`She studies you a moment longer, and whatever she finds, it isn't enough yet. “Hm,” she says, and goes back to sweeping — alone, by choice, the gap between you exactly the size of the truth you didn't tell her on the night of the knot.`)+P(`There is something she isn't giving you. You can feel the held-back weight of it, like a door with a hand flat against the other side.`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Winter work waits, and so does your art. Choose your study.`,do:()=>{if(G.sho>=2)addIns(2);},go:"a1c4_study"}]};

SC["a1c4_study"]={t:()=>P(`The woodshed hours sharpen. You can hold a knot now without watching it, snare a falling ladle out of the air, stitch a cracked bucket-stave so it holds water and looks like luck. But Snare Knot is one word, and a language needs more. The lengthening autumn evenings are yours; what you can master before the snows is one true Pattern.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Razor Thread — a stretched thread, plucked, becomes an edge. Offense.`,do:()=>{learn("razor","Razor Thread");},go:"a1c5_audit"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Mirror Lattice — a woven net that catches force and throws it back. Defense.`,do:()=>{learn("mirror","Mirror Lattice");},go:"a1c5_audit"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Mend Weave — flesh is cloth. Torn cloth can be rewoven. Healing.`,do:()=>{learn("mend","Mend Weave");},go:"a1c5_audit"}]};